WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.098
- So, you've also got a
new movie, "Songbird."

00:00:02.098 --> 00:00:02.931
- I do.

00:00:02.931 --> 00:00:03.990
- You are constantly working, girl.

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:06.320
Okay. So how did you do
all of this in a pandemic?

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:08.250
- I'm so grateful.

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:11.650
I was able to shoot the first movie

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:13.470
ever to be shot during a global pandemic,

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:14.360
which is incredible.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:17.160
And I remember, recently
I came home from work,

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:18.460
and there was a package at the door,

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:20.100
which we know is really
exciting right now,

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:20.933
when we get packages.

00:00:20.933 --> 00:00:22.468
- Yeah, yeah, like Christmas.

00:00:22.468 --> 00:00:23.900
- And it was from our producers,

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:26.230
from Michael Bay and my
director, Adam Mason.

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:30.600
And it was a t-shirt with
the first slate of the movie.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:32.980
And they said that this
slate will go down in history

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:35.250
as the first film to ever
be shot during a pandemic.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:36.310
So, it's incredible.

00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:37.350
I feel so honored.

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:40.880
- Wow. And you're, speaking
of all of this also,

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:42.500
on a really cool human note,

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.820
you're now a new, you're an
ambassador for UNICEF, right?

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:46.180
- For UNICEF, yes. Yes.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:47.371
- That's crazy.

00:00:47.371 --> 00:00:48.204
So, how did that come about

00:00:48.204 --> 00:00:49.360
and what exactly does that entail?

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:50.739
Does it kind of happen after

00:00:50.739 --> 00:00:52.930
you're allowed to start traveling again?

00:00:52.930 --> 00:00:55.200
- Yes. Well, I've been supporting UNICEF

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.240
for a few years now,
and this also goes back

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:59.020
to my mom when I was young.

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:00.490
She always kind of instilled in us

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:02.030
that the most important
thing that we can do

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:03.330
is to give back.

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:05.280
And she would always
refer to Audrey Hepburn,

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:08.400
who was the first UNICEF
ambassador, and who's like my icon.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.530
And now to be, to join those ranks

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:12.470
and to be able to be a UNICEF ambassador

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:15.300
is the most important
thing that I'll ever do.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:16.250
And I'm so honored.

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:19.410
And it basically means, yes,
I do get to go on field trips,

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:21.550
and I once traveled to Brazil with them.

00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:22.720
And I see firsthand, like,

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:23.675
the schools that they're building,

00:01:23.675 --> 00:01:26.690
the girls that they actually
save through education,

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:29.270
which is kind of like where my heart lies.

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:30.740
And I'm just so thrilled to see

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:31.940
where this journey will take us.

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:33.403
- Me as well.

00:01:33.403 --> 00:01:34.240
I think it's really key,
too, like, right now,

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:36.730
because I have kids, and
my mom was a teacher.

00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:38.660
And it, education is so important.

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:40.180
And we take it for
granted in this country.

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:41.013
- Because we don't have to think about it.

00:01:41.013 --> 00:01:43.132
- It's offered, because
we don't think about it.

00:01:43.132 --> 00:01:43.965
And now that our kids are,

00:01:43.965 --> 00:01:45.584
my kids are dying to go to school.

00:01:45.584 --> 00:01:46.417
- [Sofia] How beautiful is that?

00:01:46.417 --> 00:01:48.200
- Like, my little boy is
actually already able to go,

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:49.820
but my little girl is
dying to physically, like,

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:50.653
be in school.

00:01:50.653 --> 00:01:51.650
- 'Cause they know what it's like to not.

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:52.830
- 'Cause they, now they
know what it's like

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:53.760
to not have that.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:55.730
And it's been kind of taken away.

